cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Evergreen Common Lisp in research, benchmarks, or published work,
  please cite the software using this metadata.
title: Evergreen Common Lisp
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Green
    given-names: Anthony
version: 0.0.1
repository-code: https://github.com/atgreen/evergreen
url: https://atgreen.github.io/evergreen/
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  Evergreen Common Lisp (EGCL) is an experimental Common Lisp implementation
  written in Rust. It combines bytecode execution, tiered native compilation,
  on-stack replacement, speculative optimization, a precise moving garbage
  collector, lightweight fibers, foreign-language interoperability, and saved
  application images. It is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later with the
  Classpath Exception 2.0.
keywords:
  - Common Lisp
  - compiler
  - just-in-time compilation
  - virtual machine
  - garbage collection
